[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3955244394","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115738#issuecomment-3955244394","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115738","id":3955244394,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rwD1q","user":{"login":"jaydensipe","id":47132280,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTMyMjgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47132280?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe","html_url":"https://github.com/jaydensipe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-24T23:10:37Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T23:12:01Z","body":"> * Wait around 30 seconds to a minute.\r\n> \r\n> The crash doesn't occur on `master`, but note the issue below that occurred in `master`.\r\n> \r\n> On the bright side, this PR seems to fix not being able to assign objects to properties while in the remote inspector. Previously, it would revert to `<null>` shortly after you assign an object and print this:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> ERROR: Resource file not found: res://::kujrx (expected type: unknown)\r\n>    at: _load (core/io/resource_loader.cpp:351)\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nFixed the crash, but this does return it to main's functionality, of where the object will revert back to _null_, but I believe that was an unintended side effect of this change. The crash was because when you did assign that object, it was null, so I believe an actual fix to that will require more work.\r\n\r\nAlso cc @YeldhamDev as I know he's been working on this area and to make sure he likes this approach.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3955244394/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3959806293","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115738#issuecomment-3959806293","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115738","id":3959806293,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sBdlV","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-25T14:51:39Z","updated_at":"2026-02-25T14:51:39Z","body":"I noticed that if you have a `@export` variable that is set via the inspector, it will show the variable's type instead of the node's:\r\n|Editor|Runtime|\r\n|-|-|\r\n|<img width=\"309\" height=\"74\" alt=\"Screenshot_20260225_114748\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2068c8d3-99fb-4e4a-9165-fcfdb06f6a6a\" />|<img width=\"309\" height=\"74\" alt=\"Screenshot_20260225_114814\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1d2241bc-09db-4b2b-b9fb-73f7c565e4ff\" />|","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3959806293/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4020487190","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115738#issuecomment-4020487190","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115738","id":4020487190,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7vo8QW","user":{"login":"jaydensipe","id":47132280,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTMyMjgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47132280?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe","html_url":"https://github.com/jaydensipe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-09T01:11:28Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T04:07:29Z","body":"> I noticed that if you have a `@export` variable that is set via the inspector, it will show the variable's type instead of the node's:\r\n> \r\n> Editor\tRuntime\r\n> <img alt=\"Screenshot_20260225_114748\" width=\"309\" height=\"74\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/30739239/554812737-2068c8d3-99fb-4e4a-9165-fcfdb06f6a6a.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..YL2Y5A3OtkjCLIc3Lrmz3A0gKRIVW74HQ8sknWm08y4\">\t<img alt=\"Screenshot_20260225_114814\" width=\"309\" height=\"74\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/30739239/554812958-1d2241bc-09db-4b2b-b9fb-73f7c565e4ff.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..HurioBAm_lMdvpjiyUL_yqugBdYW3-8f5-kq3gj4GW0\">\r\n\r\n@YeldhamDev Yo, so I've been digging through this and am unsure where to proceed, as this is an issue from this piece of code (**scene_debugger_object.cpp:75**):\r\n```c++\r\n// Add base object properties.\r\nList<PropertyInfo> pinfo;\r\np_obj->get_property_list(&pinfo, true);\r\nfor (const PropertyInfo &E : pinfo) {\r\n    if (E.usage & (PROPERTY_USAGE_EDITOR | PROPERTY_USAGE_CATEGORY)) {\r\n\t    properties.push_back(SceneDebuggerProperty(E, p_obj->get(E.name)));\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\nThis passes back the base class because that is what is returned in `get_property_list()`.\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\n@onready var decal_spawn_component_3d: Node3D = $DecalSpawnComponent3D\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe above example (setting var type as Node3D, but assigning DecalSpawnComponent3D), for instance, works because it is passed through my code (the stuff that handles Members/, Constants/, Node/, etc.) , which grabs the name from the Script. The nodes which are not apart of the Members/ do not go through this code, and therefore take the base class from the get_property_list().\r\n\r\nI may be looking at this wrong, as I don't want to modify too much, but perhaps there is a better idea?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4020487190/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4024067417","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115738#issuecomment-4024067417","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115738","id":4024067417,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7v2mVZ","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-09T14:10:36Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T14:10:36Z","body":"From a glance, it seems that the way to extract the real class name would be similar.\r\nSince this would the the third place where it happens, I would also try turning it into an internal helper function to ease on code duplication, if possible.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4024067417/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"e